			<div class="content" id="post-content-3779048">
									

<p>This one is dedicated to my stepdad, who loves wine and hates reading instruction manuals.</p>
<p>Image Credit: public domain image from <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Splendor_Solis_-_Kupferstichkabinett_Berlin_78D3#/media/File:Splendor_Solis_22_sun_rising_over_city.jpg">here</a>, modified by me.</p>
<p>Thanks to ModernMajorGeneral in chat for reading over this!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Spoilers/Commentary</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I honestly haven't decided whether these wine bottles actually come from Alagadda or that's the marketing angle MC&amp;D have decided to use. I might write a MCD-format article that explains that, either as the result of a (possibly millenia-long) trade agreement with one of the Masked Lords or as a clever marketing trick to spin some boring old blood rituals into something more exotic.</p>
<p>Originally this actually was going to be about a millenia-old relationship between MCD and Alagadda, but then Enzo appeared and I decided to cut all the ancient stuff about transport amphorae and ancient Roman religion. Thanks Enzo.</p>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
